{
	title: 'Web uses locally bundled IBM Plex Mono Regular',
	spec: 'The main web UI uses locally served IBM Plex Mono, with Regular 400 and Bold 700 as the tracked defaults and corresponding italic faces. Git tracks the app font files, so a fresh checkout serves real fonts; other WOFF2 and TTF files are gitignored. scripts/fonts downloads the four default faces from IBM/plex master packages/plex-mono/fonts/complete/woff2, or selected known face names supplied as arguments, and preserves existing files if downloads fail. Tracked licenses ship beside them: src/web/fonts/OFL.txt for Plex and src/web/fonts/SourceCodePro-OFL.txt for Source Code Pro; the font files stay unmodified so their reserved names remain usable. Same-origin font routes serve known face names as font/woff2 with caching. There are no third-party browser font requests or automatic network downloads. Body, controls and Markdown code share the family; terminal fonts stay unchanged. Experimental weights and italic alternatives remain local until selected.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Assets downloaded unmodified from IBM/plex master, packages/plex-mono/fonts/complete/woff2, with the repository LICENSE.txt. All four same-origin routes returned HTTP 200, font/woff2 and wOF2 signatures. Focused web suite had 17 passes and 36 failures: a host-mode event expectation mismatch and Chromium startup timeouts prevented browser verification.',
		'Fonts were briefly gitignored by temporary guidance against heavy binaries; a fresh download then had no web fonts. Track only the app faces (about 219 KB); demo fonts stay local.'
